<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Aerial jump hardware extends the Breach Jump.
    VFEP's Aerial shoulders and helmet carry VFEP_PowerJumpRange offsets (+5 and +10) that
    only the Aerial set's own Power Jump reads, so at the foundry an Aerial helmet or pauldron
    on a Shipcracker armor added nothing to its jump. This mirrors those two offsets onto
    SCWC_BreachJumpRange, the stat Ability_BreachJump reads, so the shoulder thrusters and the
    helmet's jump telemetry (VFEP's own description of the piece) work on either engine. With
    both the breach jump reaches 35, still under Aerial's own 40. The reverse is deliberately
    absent: breaching arms and a respirator are not jump hardware, and the set's range lives
    on the armor (see StatDefs/BreachJumpRange.xml).
    Both xpaths match on the VFEP_PowerJumpRange leaf these defs declare directly, so the
    patch is independent of VFEP's abstract bases. Vanilla equippedStatOffsets add across
    worn pieces; no C# and no DefInjected point is involved.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Aerial"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
    <value>
      <SCWC_BreachJumpRange>5</SCWC_BreachJumpRange>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Aerial"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
    <value>
      <SCWC_BreachJumpRange>10</SCWC_BreachJumpRange>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
